id: pm-idj82e
title: Prevent dogfood telemetry workers from recreating disposable workspaces
description: Real package-first acceptance passed but a detached telemetry worker recreated its deleted root with global settings and telemetry state. Disable telemetry in this synthetic acceptance environment so its processes cannot outlive the owned root; keep production telemetry verification in dedicated acceptance and live gates.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-22T10:05:21.251Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:49.750Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:48.605Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:48.605Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Child invocations explicitly disable synthetic telemetry even when the parent enables it; real package-first acceptance passes and its root stays absent; production telemetry gates remain enabled and pass
parent: pm-p5u6
resolution: Package-first acceptance explicitly disables telemetry in every synthetic child invocation; production telemetry behavior is unchanged.
expected_result: The package-authoring journey completes without a detached telemetry worker recreating its deleted workspace.
actual_result: "The existing success-path regression fails before the fix and passes afterward; all 39 unit cases and the real 89-command journey pass, and its root remains absent."
